# Live-session-only packages of the cham3 M1 image (installed in live-build's "live"
# pass; the image's debian-installer removes them from an installed system).
#
# user-setup: live-config creates the live account ("user", live-config's public
# default password "live") only when this package is installed (its 0030-user-setup
# component exits early otherwise), and SDDM's live autologin into the Plasma Wayland
# session (live-config 0085-sddm plus cham3's 0086-cham3-sddm-wayland) needs that
# account. It is only a Recommends of live-config, and the image is built with
# --apt-recommends false, so without this list the first native M1 image booted to
# the SDDM greeter with no live user (VM gate, m1_image run 38203029813).
user-setup
